 "issue": 1939,
 "issue_title": "Bug: ArFrame string output is blank for zero-column frames",
 "issue_body": "## Summary\n\n`ArFrame.__str__()` renders blank table lines for frames that have rows but zero columns.\n\nThis is separate from the existing `preview()` issue: `__str__()` has its own formatting path and currently produces a confusing multi-line output with empty header, separator, and data rows.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nZero-column frames can occur after column selection, dropping all constant/empty columns, or constructing from a pandas DataFrame with an index but no columns. `str(frame)` is the default CLI/debugging representation, so it should clearly describe this valid state instead of printing blank rows.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `arnio/frame.py`: `ArFrame.__str__()` only special-cases `rows == 0`.\n- For `rows > 0` and `cols == 0`, `col_header`, `separator`, and each row render as empty strings.\n\n## Reproduction or trigger\n\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\nimport arnio as ar\n\nframe = ar.from_pandas(pd.DataFrame(index=range(2)))\nprint(frame.shape)      # (2, 0)\nprint(str(frame))\n```\n\nCurrent output includes blank table lines:\n\n```text\nArFrame: 2 rows \u00d7 0 columns\nColumns: []\nDTypes: {}\nMemory: 104 bytes\n\n\n\n```\n\n## Expected behavior\n\n`str(frame)` should explicitly report the state, for example:\n\n```text\nArFrame: 2 rows \u00d7 0 columns\nColumns: []\nDTypes: {}\nMemory: ... bytes\n(no columns to display)\n```\n\n## Actual behavior\n\nThe representation prints empty header/separator/data lines, which looks like broken output.\n\n## Suggested direction\n\nAdd a `cols == 0` branch in `ArFrame.__str__()` before building table rows. Add a regression test for a non-empty zero-column frame.\n\n## References\n\n- `arnio/frame.py`: `ArFrame.__str__()`\n- Related but separate display path: #1401 covers `ArFrame.preview()`",
 "issue_url": "https://github.com/im-anishraj/arnio/issues/1939",
 "pr": 2033,
 "pr_title": "fix: ArFrame string output is blank for zero-column frames",
 "pr_body": "Implemented the fix and regression test.\r\n\r\n### Changes made\r\n- Added a zero-column fast path in frame.py so non-empty frames with 0 columns no longer render blank table lines.\r\n- The string output now includes an explicit terminal line, shown at frame.py: (no columns to display).\r\n- Added regression test test_frame.py for a frame with 2 rows and 0 columns, asserting the shape line, columns, dtypes, and explicit no-columns message.\r\n\r\n### Validation\r\n- Ran targeted pytest for string tests in test_frame.\r\n- Test run could not proceed because collection fails before tests execute: arnio._arnio_cpp is missing in this environment, so importing arnio fails.\r\n- Error summary: ModuleNotFoundError for arnio._arnio_cpp, then ImportError from _core.py during test collection.\r\n\r\ncloses #1939",
 "fix_commit": "2070b3925aca203c3699f8b666a5edb002fcfc91",
